Same Tree
Approach

Recursively compare two trees node by node:

If both nodes are null → same (base case)
If only one is null → different
If values don't match → different
Otherwise, recursively check left subtrees and right subtrees — both must match (&&, not ||)
Code
cpp
class Solution {
public:
    bool isSameTree(TreeNode* p, TreeNode* q) {
        if (p == nullptr && q == nullptr) return true;
        if (p == nullptr || q == nullptr) return false;
        if (p->val != q->val) return false;
        return isSameTree(p->left, q->left) && isSameTree(p->right, q->right);
    }
};

Complexity
Time: O(n) — every node visited once
Space: O(h) — recursion stack, h = height of tree (O(log n) balanced, O(n) skewed)
Notes
Null checks must come before ->val access, else null pointer dereference.
&& is required in the final return — both subtrees must match, not just one.